<title>USA: Citgo to restart unit at Texas refinery next week.</title>
<headline>Citgo to restart unit at Texas refinery next week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citgo Petroleum Corp said it will restart the 21,000 barrel per day alkylation unit at its Corpus Christi, Texas refinery next week.</p>
<p>The unit has been down since a fire May 12 at the refinery, which has an estimated capacity of 132,500 bpd.</p>
<p>Citgo Petroleum Corp. is owned by PDV America Inc, a subsidiary of Petroleos de Venezuela SA, the state oil company.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
